  nonce: b01e  # b01e
  message: "BEARING FROM WI-nasil (branch jgstern-agent/fix/nasil, commit a2e2534e5d, local, not yet integrated). Status unchanged.\n\nThe WI-nasil branch decides the model as ONE export Symbol per exported variable per file, and in doing so handles TWO of this row's four shapes, because they are operands of the same export statement:\n  export A=1 B=2 -> A and B (every literal operand is read now)\n  bare export X  -> X\nplus export -f / export -n (no variable: functions / un-export) and export -p (inert), with options read only up to -- or the first operand (GNU bash 5.2.21 behaviour, verified).\nMeasured on 29 corpus repos: 921 (path,name) export pairs gained, 0 lost.\n\nSTILL OPEN HERE: declare -x / typeset -x / local -x (they export, but inside a function they make the variable function-LOCAL, which a file-scoped (path,name) export identity cannot represent -- that scope question is the decision this row now owns) and readonly R=1 (does NOT export; whether bash should emit a non-export variable/constant symbol at all is a separate modelling question). Implementation site: bash.py _exported_variable_names returns [] for any keyword other than export."  # b01e
